  "verbalization": "Lancifodilactone N is shown to have a direct target relationship with Caspase-5, which is in turn targeted by two different compounds—Robinetinidol and cholesta-5,7,8(14),22E-tetraen-3-one. Both of these compounds are linked to the CD276 antigen, suggesting a potential pathway through which Lancifodilactone N may influence CD276 expression or function. The evidence is consistent across three distinct paths, each showing a clear and direct sequence from the drug to Caspase-5 to CD276. The high final scores in all three paths indicate a strong level of confidence in this relationship. The mechanism appears to involve Caspase-5 as a critical mediator, with the drug potentially modulating its activity to affect CD276. The observed targeting of Caspase-5 by multiple compounds supports the idea that this enzyme is a key node in a broader biological network, and that Lancifodilactone N may act through a similar mechanism. The integration of these findings suggests a plausible, mechanistically sound link between Lancifodilactone N and CD276 antigen, provided further validation of the drug’s mode of action and its effects on Caspase-5 is confirmed.",
